k but  the viciousness of the grey Hulk years  later in Avengers number 684 we learned  that the cocoon didn't just change the  Hulk it killed him destructible after a  nice long well-deserved vacation from  his own violent death Bruce Banner  bought the proverbial farm once again at  the end of indestructible Hulk number 20  the series ended with a mystery an  unknown assailant shoots banner in the  back of the head on the final page  leading to the story being relaunched  with a new Hulk number one after surgery  a really long fight with the abomination  in just a tiny spoonful of Iron Man's  extremis formula the Marvel Universe is  introduced to doc green a version of the  Hulk which shares Bruce banners  intelligence but has a completely  different personality after launching a  crusade to remove the powers of  virtually every gamma-powered monster in  the Marvel Universe we finally learn who  was responsible for his attempted murder  dr. Melinda Luke and stern shot banner  but it was Betty Ross his longtime love  gave her the intelligence she needed to  pull it off after her own adventures as  the red she-hulk Ross was convinced her  former husband was going to cause an  extinction-level event in the near  future  heads up here's a Hulk death that  shouldn't count  but apparently does in Avengers Ultron  forever number one the Hulk is part of a  team of Avengers pulled from different  moments in  as soon as he enters the fray though  he's apparently decapitated by one of  Ultron's lackeys then in the issue that  follows we learned that the Hulk didn't  really lose his head he lost a mask  see the Hulk of Ultron forever is a very  early version of the Hulk pulled from  1963 s Incredible Hulk number six in  that strange issue banner transformed  into a form that had a big green Hulk  body and a little Bruce Banner head the  Hulk was forced to Don a Hulk mask to  hide his identity that's the Hulk who  shows up in Ultron forever and while  that shouldn't technicall